# =============================================================================
# Policy: what stays in git
# =============================================================================
# - Track: tests/**/*.py, tests/conftest.py (CI requires them).
# - Ignore: everything above under tests/ that is cache, Hypothesis, tmp, or coverage.
# - Do NOT add a blanket "tests/*.py" rule — that would break CI and code review.
# =============================================================================
# Local editor / tooling (repo checkout)
# =============================================================================
.cursor/
.windsurf/
**/kicad-symbols*

# =============================================================================
# Local stress-test outputs (repo root convenience)
# =============================================================================
stress_*.kicad_*
stress_*.net
stress_*.csv
stress_*.openhac-*
fc_ms_test*.kicad_*
fc_ms_test*.net
fc_ms_test*.csv
fc_ms_test*.openhac-*
scratch/
z3_cache.json

# =============================================================================
# Optional local-only trees (do NOT ignore tracked project dirs)
# =============================================================================
# Keep tests/, scripts/, examples/, seeds/ tracked for CI and docs.
# Ignore only a local root-level "database/" scratch folder if you create one
# (the package catalog lives under openhac/database/).
/database/

# =============================================================================
# Policy: what stays in git
# =============================================================================
# - Track: tests/**/*.py, tests/fixtures/** (except generated/), scripts/, examples/, seeds/
# - Ignore: caches, Hypothesis, tmp, coverage, KiCad compile artifacts (patterns above)
# - Do NOT add blanket "tests/" / "scripts/" / "examples/" rules — that hides new CI
#   fixtures and forces `git add -f` for every new file.
